Deterministic HugeTLB subpool rollback race reproducers
=======================================================

WARNING: TEST-ONLY KERNEL BRANCH

This directory and the CONFIG_HUGETLB_P4_TEST instrumentation in this
commit are for reproducing two accounting bugs in the exact v3 HugeTLB
subpool series.  Do not enable the instrumentation in a production kernel.
The parent of this commit is the full v3 series at:

  a73701d8e7667015c956581eb80659aaff8ef6de

No production fix is included.

Why kernel instrumentation is required
--------------------------------------

The races require another operation to run in two narrow windows inside
the kernel.  A default-off debugfs hook selects one PID and pauses it:

  1. after hugepage_subpool_get_pages(); and
  2. after global accounting or folio allocation fails, before rollback.

Userspace then releases and consumes reservation capacity before allowing
the target to continue.  This makes the otherwise timing-dependent races
deterministic.  The region_add() fault-injection switch inherited from the
original patch-4 test remains disabled in these tests; fail_hits must remain
zero.

Tests
-----

reservation
  Exercises the early out_put_pages rollback in hugetlb_reserve_pages().
  The ignored positive correction is +2 and returns -ENOMEM.  After file
  cleanup only two reservations back a four-page minimum; unmount produces
  ULONG_MAX - 1.

allocation
  Exercises out_subpool_put after alloc_hugetlb_folio() fails.  The ignored
  positive correction is +1 and returns -ENOMEM.  After file cleanup only
  three reservations back a four-page minimum; unmount produces ULONG_MAX.

Both tests require a fresh boot with exactly seven 2 MiB huge pages and no
overcommit.  Run each test separately; the expected counter underflow makes
the guest unsuitable for further testing after it completes.

Files
-----

  early-cleanup-proof.c       reservation userspace controller
  allocation-cleanup-proof.c allocation userspace controller
  init-reservation            minimal guest init for reservation test
  init-allocation             minimal guest init for allocation test
  validate-reservation.py     exact-value console validator
  validate-allocation.py      exact-value console validator
  mk-initramfs.sh             creates a reproducible BusyBox initramfs
  run-qemu.sh                 boots QEMU and runs the matching validator

Build the instrumented kernel
-----------------------------

Starting from the repository root, for example:

  mkdir -p build
  make O=build x86_64_defconfig
  scripts/config --file build/.config \
    -e HUGETLBFS -e DEBUG_FS -e HUGETLB_P4_TEST \
    -e BLK_DEV_INITRD -e DEVTMPFS
  make O=build olddefconfig
  make O=build -j4 bzImage usr/gen_init_cpio

Confirm that build/.config contains:

  CONFIG_HUGETLBFS=y
  CONFIG_DEBUG_FS=y
  CONFIG_HUGETLB_P4_TEST=y

Build the controllers and initramfses
-------------------------------------

A statically linked BusyBox is required.  From this directory:

  make LDFLAGS=-static

  ./mk-initramfs.sh reservation /path/to/busybox \
    /path/to/linux/build/usr/gen_init_cpio /tmp/reservation.cpio.gz

  ./mk-initramfs.sh allocation /path/to/busybox \
    /path/to/linux/build/usr/gen_init_cpio /tmp/allocation.cpio.gz

The script verifies that the selected controller is statically linked.

Run
---

Run each case at one or four vCPUs.  The runner uses TCG and validates the
retained console after the guest powers off:

  ./run-qemu.sh reservation \
    /path/to/linux/build/arch/x86/boot/bzImage \
    /tmp/reservation.cpio.gz 1 /tmp/reservation-smp1.log

  ./run-qemu.sh allocation \
    /path/to/linux/build/arch/x86/boot/bzImage \
    /tmp/allocation.cpio.gz 4 /tmp/allocation-smp4.log

Successful reproduction ends with validator JSON containing
"result": "PASS".  Here PASS means that the expected full-v3 accounting
bug was reproduced, not that the kernel is correct.

Expected observations
---------------------

                    correction       after files       after unmount
  reservation       +2, -ENOMEM      2                 ULONG_MAX - 1
  allocation        +1, -ENOMEM      3                 ULONG_MAX

The same results were retained from fresh one- and four-vCPU QEMU boots for
each case.  The hooks select only the requested target PID and include a
30-second in-kernel timeout so a controller failure does not wait forever.
